  "text": "Arc\nComponents\nBlocks\nDocs\nPricing\nTry the demo\nSearch\n⌘ K\nAppearance\nSign in\nCtrl K\nAll\nFree\nPro\nMore\nDocs\nIntroduction\nInstallation\nTheming\nMotion\nAI and MCP\nChangelog\nComponents\n125\nButtons\n10\nButton\nAction button\nSplit button\nButton group\nFloating button group\nExpanding button group\nCopy button\nIcon morph\nConfirm morph\nTheme switcher\nGestures\n3\nHold to confirm\nSwipe actions\nReactions\nMenus\n3\nDropdown menu\nContext menu\nUser menu\nText fields\n7\nInput\nTextarea\nPassword field\nPassword strength\nSearch field\nExpanding search\nInline edit\nSpecial inputs\n7\nNumber field\nMoney input\nPhone input\nScrub input\nNew\nTag input\nMention input\nShortcut recorder\nSelects\n5\nSelect\nCombobox\nMulti-select\nMorph select\nChip group\nToggles\n7\nRadio cards\nBilling toggle\nCheckbox\nRadio group\nSwitch\nSegmented control\nRating\nNew\nSliders\n2\nSlider\nElastic slider\nPickers\n6\nCalendar\nDate picker\nDate range picker\nTime picker\nColor picker\nEmoji picker\nPro\nEditors\n4\nRich text editor\nSignature pad\nFile dropzone\nAvatar upload\nPro\nNavigation\n4\nTabs\nBreadcrumb\nPagination\nMega menu morph\nPro\nExpand\n5\nScroll area\nAccordion\nExpandable card\nResizable panels\nExpandable text\nOverlays\n7\nDialog\nDrawer\nBottom sheet\nPopover\nHover card\nTooltip\nShare access\nPro\nMessages\n5\nAlert\nToast\nToast stack\nAnnouncement bar\nCookie consent\nProgress\n6\nProgress\nSkeleton\nStepper\nCountdown\nUsage meter\nOnboarding checklist\nNew\nAvatars\n4\nAvatar\nAvatar group\nBadge\nPresence stack\nPro\nCards\n3\nCard\nMetric card\nEmpty state\nCharts\n14\nLine chart\nBar chart\nDonut chart\nStreamgraph\nBrush chart\nWaffle chart\nSlope chart\nSparkline\nGauge\nActivity heatmap\nAnimated counter\nRidgeline\nTreemap\nSplit bar\nPro\nAdvanced charts\n7\nPro\nSunburst\nSankey flow\nFunnel chart\nRadar chart\nRealtime stream\nRace bar chart\nData grid\nTables\n6\nSortable data table\nTree view\nReorderable list\nNew\nFilter toolbar\nCode block\nJSON viewer\nActivity\n3\nTimeline\nComment thread\nChat thread\nMedia\n3\nImage compare\nCarousel\nCard stack\nText effects\n4\nText reveal\nIn-view title\nText morph\nText shimmer\nBlocks\n102\nSpecial components\n54\nWhat’s new\n31 new\nComponents\nButton\nButton\n\nA clear, responsive action with quiet secondary states.\n\n$\npnpm dlx shadcn@latest add @uiarc/button\nCopy page\nCopied\nCopy failed\nPreview\nCode\nLive · keyboard ready\nStyles\nSave changes\nSecondary\nGhost\nDelete\nIcons and sizes\nAdd item\nContinue\nLarge\nFeedback and states\nCopy link\nUpload file\nDisabled\nWhen to use\nAny single action on a page, form, or dialog, such as Save, Continue, or Cancel.\nActions whose label changes in place, like Save to Saved, where the width should spring instead of jump.\nShort async work where a spinner on the button is enough feedback, via loading.\nWhen not to use\nUse action-button when the button itself should show pending and success states after an async commit.\nUse split-button when one default action has two to five close variants.\nUse hold-to-confirm for destructive actions that need more than a single click.\nInstallation\n\nAdd Button with the shadcn CLI, or copy the source by hand.\n\nCLI\nManual\npnpm\nnpm\nyarn\nbun\nCopy\nCopied\nFailed\n$\npnpm dlx shadcn@latest add @uiarc/button\npnpm dlx shadcn@latest add @uiarc/button\n\nAdds the component and its local dependencies, and installs motion. First time? Add the @uiarc registry to components.json, or use the full URL:\n\npnpm dlx shadcn@latest add https://uiarc.dev/r/button.json\nUsage\nexample.tsx\nCopy\nCopied\nFailed\n1\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/arc/button/button\";\n2\n \n3\nexport function SaveBar() {\n4\n  return (\n5\n    <Button variant=\"primary\" loading={saving} onClick={save}>\n6\n      Save changes\n7\n    </Button>\n8\n  );\n9\n}\nExamples\nLabel that morphs after saving\nexample.tsx\nCopy\nCopied\nFailed\n1\n<Button variant=\"secondary\" loading={saving} onClick={save}>\n2\n  {saved ? \"Saved\" : \"Save draft\"}\n3\n</Button>\nAPI reference\nButton\n\nA native button with press feedback and a label that morphs its width when the content changes.\n\nProp\nType\nDefault\nDescription\nvariant\n\"primary\" | \"secondary\" | \"ghost\" | \"danger\"\n\"primary\"\nVisual weight. Use one primary action per surface.\nsize\n\"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\"\n\"md\"\nHeight and padding.\nloading\nboolean\nfalse\nShows a spinner, sets aria-busy, and swallows clicks while keeping focus.\n...props\nButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>\n–\nForwarded to the underlying button, including ref, disabled, type, and onClick.\nKeyboard interactions\nEnter\nor\nSpace\nActivates the button.\nAccessibility\nRenders a native button, so role and focus come for free.\nLoading uses aria-busy and aria-disabled instead of disabled, so keyboard focus is not lost mid-action.\nIcon-only buttons need an aria-label.\nDisabled primary buttons fade as a whole. Disabled secondary and danger buttons keep their border and take a muted fill and label, and disabled ghost buttons take a muted label, so an unavailable action still reads as a button.\nMotion\nPresses scale to about 0.97 on a snappy spring; icon-sized buttons press slightly deeper.\nA new label crossfades with a short blur while the width springs to fit.\nReduced motion drops the press scale and swaps labels with a plain fade.\nResponsive behavior\nSize is fixed by the size prop; the button never changes layout by breakpoint, so pick lg for primary touch targets.\nHover styles apply only on hover-capable fine pointers, so taps on touch screens do not stick in a hover state.\nPerformance\nA ResizeObserver measures the label so the width can spring; one per button is cheap, but avoid hundreds in a long list.\nLabel changes animate opacity, transform, and a small blur only, with no layout thrash beyond the width spring.\nNotes for AI\n\nGive your coding assistant the Markdown reference instead of screenshots.\n\nDefault choice for any single action. Use action-button for dense icon toolbars and split-button when one action has close alternatives.\nPass a changing label (Save → Saved) as children to get the width morph for free.\nWrap in a Radix trigger with asChild; the press scale turns off automatically for popup anchors.\n/components/button/markdown\nCopy URL\nCopied\nFailed\n\nThe full library index for assistants is at /llms.txt.\n\nRelated\nAction button\nComponent\nA compact button for frequent toolbar actions.\nSplit button\nComponent\nA primary action with a menu of nearby alternatives.\nCopy button\nComponent\nCopy a value with immediate confirmation.\nHold to confirm\nComponent\nConfirm a destructive action by holding, not tapping.\nNext\nAction button\nArc · 182 components\nllms.txt\n\nOn this page\n\nPreview\nWhen to use\nWhen not to use\nInstallation\nUsage\nExamples\nAPI reference\nKeyboard\nAccessibility\nMotion\nResponsive behavior\nPerformance\nNotes for AI\nRelated\nView as Markdown\nBack to top\n66 motion components, plus every block and template. One payment, new releases included.\nArc Pro\nSee Pro",
